jt-pve-storage-dellemc (0.7.66~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * BETA RELEASE. Not for production use.
  * MULTIPATH: every successful delete printed a failure that had not
    happened - "multipath -f /dev/mapper/... failed or timed out, trying
    dmsetup remove --force", twice per qm destroy on the ME4024.
    cleanup_lun_devices removes the map by name first and then calls the
    flush as the belt to that pair of braces; multipath -f on a map that is
    already gone exits non-zero. The flush now checks whether the device is
    still there before saying anything: gone is what was being asked for.
    Anything else, including not being able to tell, still gets the dmsetup
    fallback - a stat that times out on a dead map is exactly the state that
    fallback exists for. A line on every normal operation reads like a fault
    and buries the case where the flush really did time out.
  * The project no longer claims that no hardware has run it. A PowerVault
    ME4024 has, over Fibre Channel, and as of 0.7.65 it passes the whole
    first-run test. The README, the docs site, the phase table and the
    release notes said otherwise in five places. What is still unverified is
    stated instead: PowerStore and PowerFlex entirely, and PowerVault's
    iSCSI and SAS paths.
  * The release notes explain why no release carries GitHub's "Latest"
    badge - every 0.x is a prerelease, and GitHub will not mark a prerelease
    latest - and give a command that resolves the newest release with
    prereleases included.

