jt-pve-storage-dellemc (0.7.48~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * BETA RELEASE. Not for production use. No storage type has been run
    against physical hardware.
  * PowerFlex had no in-use check anywhere. It does not inherit BlockBase, so
    none of the guards the SAN families have applied to it: free_image
    unmapped and deleted a volume, create_base captured a template, and
    volume_snapshot_rollback overwrote a volume, none of them testing whether
    a guest was using it. All three now refuse both when the device is in use
    and when that cannot be established.
  * PowerFlex rollback flushes the host cache before the array restores the
    snapshot and invalidates it after, as the SAN families do.
  * The ownership gate now runs in front of PowerFlex's deletes too.
  * CLAUDE.md records every defect found in this audit, and adds a data-safety
    checklist of the questions that found them.

