jt-pve-storage-dellemc (0.7.47~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * BETA RELEASE. Not for production use. No storage type has been run
    against physical hardware.
  * PowerVault: a volume name can no longer act as a shell wildcard. The URL
    escaping left *, ? and [] unescaped in EVERY argument because 'show
    volumes pattern' needs them in one. 'delete volumes' takes its target
    positionally, so a name of 'pve-me5-*' would have asked the array to
    delete every volume of the storage. Only the argument after the literal
    'pattern' token keeps its wildcards now.
  * The temporary-clone reaper required only that a name start with this
    storage's prefix - which every VM disk on the storage also does. A record
    naming a real disk was enough to delete it, unattended, in the background
    of a poll. A temporary clone is now identified by the infix its name
    carries, which no VM disk has.

