jt-pve-storage-dellemc (0.7.46~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * BETA RELEASE. Not for production use. No storage type has been run
    against physical hardware.
  * The three remaining callers of the in-use check now refuse on "could not
    tell" as well:
    - deactivate_storage removed the local devices AND unmapped the volume,
      so a wrong "free" took the disk away from a guest still writing to it.
      Disabling a storage is a thing an operator does while VMs run.
    - create_base: every linked clone reads from the marker snapshot taken
      there, so a template captured mid-write is a filesystem that was never
      consistent, copied into every clone of it.
    - The orphan reaper leaves a device alone rather than removing one it
      could not clear. It runs unattended in the background of a poll;
      leaving one for a human is free, removing one that was in use is not.
  * t/11-imports.t fails on is_device_in_use used as a bare boolean. undef
    reads as false there, which is the whole bug. The one place that is
    harmless - deciding whether to flush before a snapshot - now says why at
    the call site.

