jt-pve-storage-dellemc (0.7.44~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * BETA RELEASE. Not for production use. No storage type has been run
    against physical hardware.
  * An unreachable array made a delete report success. free_image checked
    whether the volume existed inside an eval and read any failure as "it may
    already have been deleted", then returned success. PVE removes the disk
    from the VM configuration when free_image returns - so an array that was
    briefly unreachable would have left the volume on the array with nothing
    in PVE pointing at it. The data is intact and unreachable, which is the
    worst shape a storage bug can take. "Not there" and "could not ask" are
    now different answers.
  * PowerFlex had the same hole one level deeper: the fallback volume listing
    swallowed its own error and returned an empty list, which reads as
    "absent".
  * The config-backup volume is the only device this plugin writes to, and it
    is now checked twice before mkfs: the kernel's own identification of the
    device (dm uuid, or the NAA in an sd device's wwid attribute / VPD 0x83)
    must confirm the WWID, and the device must be small enough to be a 1 MB
    config volume. Anything unconfirmed is refused; a skipped config backup
    is already non-fatal.

