jt-pve-storage-dellemc (0.7.43~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * BETA RELEASE. Not for production use. No storage type has been run
    against physical hardware.
  * The ownership gate is now actually a gate. is_pve_managed_volume was
    defined, documented as guarding every destructive path, tested directly -
    and called from nowhere. It now runs in front of every array-side delete
    of a volume or a snapshot, with the storeid, on the family's own naming
    class. Wiring it in immediately showed its own definition was incomplete:
