jt-pve-storage-dellemc (0.7.42~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * BETA RELEASE. Not for production use. No storage type has been run
    against physical hardware.
  * No multipath operation touches a map this plugin does not own, except
    one that cannot be narrowed. 'multipathd reconfigure' re-reads every
    configuration file and reapplies it to every map on the node - other
    vendors' storage included - and it was being used to make a newly-mapped
    LUN appear: on a timer in activate_storage, and on every device wait.
    Both are gone. A new LUN is claimed with 'multipathd add path <sdX>' for
    the paths of that one WWID.
  * The remaining reconfigure runs only after this plugin's own conf.d
    drop-in changes, because multipathd has no per-file reload, and it now
    says in the log that it is node-wide and why.
  * make check-multipath-flush also fails the build on the multipathd form
    of a node-wide flush, which this plugin must never generate: it removes
    every unused map on the node, other vendors' storage included.
  * A test asserts exactly one node-wide reconfigure remains in BlockBase.
  * A helper added in this work duplicated one the module already had, which
    Perl resolves by keeping the last and warning on every load - once per
    pvesm call. The duplicate is gone (the existing one is vendor-gated and
    strictly better) and t/11-imports.t now fails on any subroutine defined
    twice in a file.

