jt-pve-storage-dellemc (0.7.15~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * BETA RELEASE. Not for production use. No storage type has been run
    against physical hardware.
  * 'map volume' is the one PowerVault command whose documented argument order
    differs between ME4 and ME5, and both orders come from Dell's own CLI
    Reference: ME5 puts the volume last, ME4 puts it first. The plugin sends
    the ME5 form and falls back to the ME4 one if the array refuses it, so
    both families work; the journal records which order an array wanted.
  * 'show volumes' now sends its parameters in the documented order.
  * The host commands corrected in 0.7.14 were re-checked against the ME5
    guide as well as the ME4 one: both families document them identically, so
    that fix is right for both.
  * docs/ARCHITECTURE.md was out of date about which tests cover the abstract
    interface and the property-declaration rule, and did not mention the
    overrides added since it was written.

