jt-pve-storage-dellemc (0.7.12~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * BETA RELEASE. Not for production use. No storage type has been run
    against physical hardware.
  * Deleting a template could never succeed on PowerStore or PowerFlex. The
    decision whether to remove the template marker was made by reading the
    array's refusal text, and both families use the same wording for "this
    volume still has a snapshot" and "something was cloned from it" — on
    PowerStore the hint this plugin appends to a 422 contains the word
    "clones" itself, so the rule matched its own text. The array decides now:
    a linked clone is a clone OF THE MARKER, so an array that still has one
    refuses to delete it, and trying is both safe and reliable.
  * Operator-facing messages end at a newline, so Perl no longer appends
    " at /usr/share/perl5/... line 1234." to them in a PVE task log.
  * New test t/18-powerflex-lifecycle.t walks a whole VM's life on PowerFlex,
    which has its own alloc, clone, snapshot and delete and was therefore not
    covered by the lifecycle test added in 0.7.11. It is what found the
    template deletion above.
  * t/11-imports.t also fails now on a die message that does not end at a
    newline.

