jt-pve-storage-dellemc (0.7.7~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * BETA RELEASE. Not for production use. No storage type has been run
    against physical hardware.
  * New test file t/14-parsing.t throws missing, renamed and wrongly typed
    fields at every parser in the plugin. Each field name in these clients is
    written from documentation rather than read off an array, so some of them
    will be wrong; what matters is that a wrong one fails safe instead of
    being acted on. It found three defects.
  * Names are anchored exactly. Perl's $ also matches immediately before a
    trailing newline, so 'vm-100-disk-0' followed by one was accepted as a
    volume name and resolved to the same array object.
  * A run of digits too long to be a vmid is no longer decoded as one. Perl
    turns it into a float, and '1e+30' would have travelled inside a volid.
  * A volume listing row that is not a hash no longer takes the process down
    with a Perl type error; the listing comes back empty instead.

