jt-pve-storage-dellemc (0.5.0~beta1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * BETA RELEASE. Not for production use. See the disclaimer in README.md:
    this has never been run against a physical Dell EMC array, a defect can
    destroy VM data or hang a node, and there is no warranty of any kind.
  * Phases 2 to 4: the dellpowerstore storage type now exists. It has NOT
    been run against a PowerStore array - see docs/TESTING.md, where every
    array-facing detail is still listed as unverified.
  * Common::BlockBase: the abstract PVE plugin base. Activation, allocation,
    device discovery and teardown, snapshots, templates, clones, the
    multipath drop-in and the background orphan reaper, all independent of
    which array is behind them.
  * PowerStore::API: REST client for volumes, snapshots, thin clones, hosts,
    mappings and the transport endpoints. Listing filters server-side and
    follows pages; LUN ids are assigned by the client rather than by the
    array, because PowerStore's REST-side sequence starts at 200 and never
    reuses an id.
  * DellPowerStorePlugin: the storage type itself.
  * bin/pve-dell-config-get: reads a VM configuration back out of the config
    backup volume written alongside each snapshot, including in recover mode
    where it talks to the array directly and never touches the PVE stack.
  * Documentation: quick start, configuration reference, architecture,
    troubleshooting, naming conventions and the hardware test matrix, all in
    English and Traditional Chinese, plus the project page under docs/.
  * 713 unit tests, none of which need an array or a device.

